Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-28-2001||02:19 PM||||I saw that car at the Battle of Gettysburg '97.  It has the whole northstar cradle in it from what I hear. I have a few pics of it.  He streatched out all the pastic panels to make it wide.  Its pretty cool.  I think it was the first time he had it out and painted.  Everyone heard that thing coming, turned around and gazed at it when it pulled in the lot!  I remember riding with Bob Schlag to this bridge for pictures.  I am in a picture with that car(well at least my back) that is floating around the internet somewhere.<P>That day I got a ride in Roger Cutters' 3800.  *sniff* Haven't been to a Fiero show since.<P>I'll post my pic of it later! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||08-28-2001||05:04 PM||||More pics please!!!!!!!  Love that rebody<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000003||MikeSchaefer||08-28-2001||05:12 PM||||Yeah, that is one cool-ass car.  Here are the pics of your back Joe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/purple1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/purple2frontspoilersideintake.jpg"> ||||reg||14
