Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||08-28-2001||05:32 PM||||The only thing that really looks out of place is the taillights- stock as stock can be.  Should've painted all the black with the purple... or something!<P>I really like the high supra-style wing, AND the trunk still opens- although it looks as though it has been rounded to clear it.<P>"This Car Wash does not guarantee aftermarket ricer wings and spoilers will not be damaged (by the mustang-owning employee drying your car at the end of the line...)"<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000007||NOS3800||08-28-2001||06:09 PM||||I can provide alittle more info. The owner is Johnathan Watts. He did all the body work and paint( you can see some runs when up close) No offense. Anyway, it is Northstar powered and he did splice in the entire front drivetrain of a Caddy to the rear. Supposedly it even has the traction control and ABS. It was from what he says 12.8's in the 1/4 mile. On one run two years ago he was in the slow down area at the end of the track and went to put the car in neutral. But he went through neutral and into reverse causing the car to 360 into a cornfield. It was out of action for a year then made a trailered appearance at show in Mechanicsburg, PA and has disappeared since.<BR>The problem I have with the story of the wreck is that you can't put a car into reverse while in motion, it usually cuts out or grinds. The wheels won't start spinning backwards would they?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@99.70 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||08-28-2001||08:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeSchaefer:<BR><B>Yeah, that is one cool-ass car.  Here are the pics of your back Joe   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mike Schaefer </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Doh!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hartz||08-28-2001||10:50 PM||||Here's some "before" pics from what I believe is the '95 show in Michigan:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic1_2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic2.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic3.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic4.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pic5.JPG"> <P>I always wondered how the car turned out.  The paint isn't necessarily to my tastes, but I always thought the body work was kind of cool.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||08-29-2001||12:43 AM||||I think it might have looked better with quarter windows. I can't stand the window scoops on my car even. <BR>It also needs a wider rear bumper made for it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||b lo 0||08-29-2001||12:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NOS3800:<BR><B>On one run two years ago he was in the slow down area at the end of the track and went to put the car in neutral. But he went through neutral and into reverse causing the car to 360 into a cornfieldThe problem I have with the story of the wreck is that you can't put a car into reverse while in motion, it usually cuts out or grinds. The wheels won't start spinning backwards would they?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Funny story...  The wheels won't spin backwards, but they definitely will lock up.  Couple of examples-I was driving along at about 45 mph last week, and my ignition started acting up.  Went to put it in neutral to rev it and keep from stalling, and the button on the shifter (aftermarket knob) was stuck in and it went right into reverse.  WHOOO!  Rear wheels stopped rotating completely for about a second and nearly put the GT into a nearby ditch.  Also, a buddy of mine has (had) a drag modified Chevy LUV truck with a really built 383 and 11-inch rear slicks.  No chute.  Came off the line after an 11.89 run and went to put it in neutral, shift interlock on his Hurst failed, the truck slid sideways, the rears bit and started to spin again, and the truck flipped 3 times before coming to a halt near the runoff ramp at Atlanta Dragway.  He spent 4 days in the hospital (thank god for rollcages) and the truck was demolished.  The engine now resides in his '90 S10.  Short story long, yes, it's possible.||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||08-29-2001||01:38 AM||||Hrm, the *entire* driveline?  The Caddy's auto tranny is, I belive, entirely electronically controled.  Including global gear selection.<P>There is even a start lockout so you don't try to start the car when it's already running!!!<P>Now, maybe this had been defeated.<P>But an *entire* driveline swap would use the stock ECU, which requires the stock Tranny computer too. so I'd think the reverse lockout would be working.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tonker||08-29-2001||02:07 AM||||Got a Question for those with window scoops: How the H*** can you see anything? I have a b**** of a time with the blind spot in my GT, but to take away even that limited visibility would kill me. Anyone else have that problem or suggestions for improving it?||||reg||5
Z||000014||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||02:34 AM||||I tried to reduce this file as much as possible.  Had to scan in @ 800dpi to get it readable.  Hopefully will be readable and nobody will hate me for a big pic.  Sombody's butt is in the way.(hehe, I said butt)  That was the whole problem...trying to get a shot of the car...everyone hovered around it.  I've got a couple of pics...1 of the big honky wrap-apround dash(sorry, I just hate that bolt on thing)<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_1.jpg">    <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Pontiaddict||08-29-2001||03:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>Got a Question for those with window scoops: How the H*** can you see anything? I have a b**** of a time with the blind spot in my GT, but to take away even that limited visibility would kill me. Anyone else have that problem or suggestions for improving it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You basially use a combination of looking through the mirrors and praying that nothing's behind you. I plan on either upgrading to a notchback or swapping the scoops back to windows (possibly tinted though).||||reg||1
